Starts a program asked for over niri's socket while the session is locked.

niri drops every action that comes over its socket while the session is
locked, Spawn included, and still answers that it handled it. A program
started then, as a session another session hands the shell is, is lost
outright: nothing starts behind the lock, nor after it. A spawn asked for
over the socket now starts behind the lock. The socket is Joel's own: only
his processes can reach it, and any of them could end the locker as
easily, so a spawn from it is no weaker a lock than the one he has. What
it starts can't show or take input: a locked session's keys go to the
lock surface, and the lock surface is all that's drawn. It's started with
no activation token, so its window can't ask for the focus it would have
once unlocked. Every other action over the socket, and every key binding,
is still refused while locked, as before.

--- a/src/ipc/server.rs
+++ b/src/ipc/server.rs
@@ -388,7 +388,21 @@
                 // Make sure some logic like workspace clean-up has a chance to run before doing
                 // actions.
                 state.niri.advance_animations();
-                state.do_action(action, false);
+                // A program started over the socket while the session is
+                // locked opens behind the lock, which keeps the keyboard
+                // and is all that's drawn, so it starts rather than being
+                // dropped. It's given no activation token, so its window
+                // can't ask for the focus it would have once unlocked.
+                // Every other action is still refused while locked.
+                match action {
+                    niri_config::Action::Spawn(command) if state.niri.is_locked() => {
+                        crate::utils::spawning::spawn(command, None);
+                    }
+                    niri_config::Action::SpawnSh(command) if state.niri.is_locked() => {
+                        crate::utils::spawning::spawn_sh(command, None);
+                    }
+                    action => state.do_action(action, false),
+                }
                 let _ = tx.send_blocking(());
             });
 
